    <string name="g1_title">Welcome to Kosher Switch</string>
    <string name="g1_text">One button turns this phone into a kosher phone, and back again.\n\nFor yourself, or for your child\'s phone.</string>
    <string name="g2_title">Two modes</string>
    <string name="g2_text">Open mode: a normal phone, with everything.\n\nKosher mode: only the apps you choose, internet only where you allow it, its own home screen and locked settings. It stays kosher even after a restart.</string>
    <string name="g3_title">One-time setup: two ways</string>
    <string name="g3_text">Android lets an app lock a phone only if it\'s set up in a special way, once.\n\nA. Easiest, no computer (the phone gets reset):\n1. Back up the phone, then factory reset it.\n2. On the first “Welcome” screen, tap the screen 6 times.\n3. Scan the Kosher Switch QR code (from the Kosher Switch web page). The phone installs and sets up the app by itself.\n\nB. Keep everything, with a computer:\n1. Settings → About phone → Software information → tap “Build number” 7 times.\n2. Developer options → turn on “USB debugging”.\n3. Settings → Accounts → remove all accounts for a moment.\n4. Connect to a computer and run:\nadb shell dpm set-device-owner dev.kosherswitch/.KosherAdmin\n5. Add your accounts back.</string>
    <string name="g3_done">✓ Already done on this phone. You can skip this step.</string>
    <string name="g4_title">A secret code</string>
    <string name="g4_text">The code is the only way back to open mode.\n\nParents: choose a code your child doesn\'t know.</string>
    <string name="g5_title">Choose the apps</string>
    <string name="g5_text">Switch on the apps that stay in kosher mode, and which of them may use the internet (for example Waze).\n\nEverything else disappears until you switch back. The Settings app is always locked.</string>
    <string name="g6_title">Switching</string>
    <string name="g6_text">To turn it on: swipe down from the top and tap כשר.\nTo leave: tap כשר again and enter the code.\n\nDon\'t see the כשר button? Swipe down twice, tap ✎ (edit) and drag כשר into the panel.</string>
    <string name="g7_title">Everything is included</string>
    <string name="g7_text">The Siddur, the calendar and prayer times, Notes and the Assistant are all part of this one app. There\'s nothing else to install; they just have their own icons.\n\nOnly the Assistant\'s offline AI (1.6 GB) is an optional download, over Wi-Fi.</string>
    <string name="g8_title">You\'re ready</string>
    <string name="g8_text">Set your code, choose apps, and turn it on.</string>
